[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   Step 128 -- Post-2017 two-leg refit: the masking discriminator.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   The registered prospective test (step_117) returned a reversed
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   declared-axis contrast on the post-2017 SBDB cohort -- but the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   carrier audit showed the slip observable is structurally absent from
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   single-solution records: a joint fit absorbs any uniform proper-time
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   slip into shared orbital elements, leaving the propagated residual
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   dominated by planetary scatter.  The holdout could therefore only
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   fail in form, never confirm: the construction needed to express the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   anomaly (a leg-separated record) does not exist in that lineage.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   Step 127 supplied the missing instrument -- an independent
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   Levenberg-Marquardt two-leg refit of the raw MPC astrometry under the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   identical REBOUND/IAS15 + DE440s force model, propagated to the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   +/-250 AU sphere through the same machinery.  On the pre-2018 cohort
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   it reproduced the catalogue record at per-comet concordance rho =
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   +0.998 and recovered the registered inbound-leg in-cap excess.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   This step points the same instrument at the post-2017 cohort
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   (step_b81 primaries).  Two constructions are tested on identical
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   members:
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   * the single-fit construction -- the propagated boundary products
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   of the joint (full-arc) fit, the only construction a
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   single-solution lineage can express.  Predicted flat under the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   masking hypothesis.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   * the leg-fit construction -- the independently fitted inbound and
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   outbound legs, whose boundary asymptotes carry whatever slip the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   transit actually imparted.  This is the construction the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   three-leg catalogue records realize, and the registered carrier
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   d_in on the pre-2018 record lives here.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   Registered tests
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   T1  instrument validity on the new era: per-comet concordance of
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   our drot versus the catalogue-propagated drot, and element
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   agreement of our full-arc fit against the SBDB seed.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   T2  DECISIVE -- the masking discriminator: on the dual-leg subset,
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   the cap contrast (theta < 60 deg, aph against the declared
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   axis) of the leg-fit inbound deviation d_in_leg versus (a) the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   single-fit d_in on the same members and (b) the catalogue's
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   propagated d_in.  Under TEP-with-masking the leg-fit channel
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   carries the in-cap excess the joint construction erases.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   Flatness on the leg-fit channel would confine the anomaly to
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   the pre-2018 era -- a substantive boundary on the hypothesis.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   T3  displaced-structure control: the same contrasts evaluated
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   about the post-2017 displaced axis (120, -40) -- does the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   modern residual systematic appear on independent fits, or was
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   it a single-lineage fit field?
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   T4  quality strata: contrast on NG-flagged vs clean comets (the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   non-gravitational floor differs by construction), and the
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   cross-arc extrapolation penalty by cap.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   T4b signature-class audit: at both axes on the dual-leg cohort,
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   cap contrasts on every channel -- leg deviations (d_in_leg,
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   d_out_leg), drot, ddirf, |daa| energy, plus coverage and
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   fit-quality controls.  The declared anomaly's class is
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   single-leg rotation slip without energy exchange; the audit
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   asks whether the displaced structure shares that class.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   T4c robustness: label-permutation nulls on the carrying channels,
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   500-direction shuffle extremeness of the displaced residual
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   gap on the independent record, and quality strata (n_obs,
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   fit RMS, NG-clean) on the same field.
[2026-09-20 12:23:45 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 128]   T5  audit: cohort yield, leg coverage, fit quality.
